    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (70.33) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.94). **Kyle Tucker** remains the anchor of the lineup, as he benefits from a favorable matchup against Brandon Sproat (xERA 4.25) and a solid spot in the four-hole. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages a strong park factor and a manageable matchup against M. Keller to drive his elite score. We are also monitoring the \"steal-heavy\" potential of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** against F. Valdez; while Valdez presents a tougher SP skill profile (3.84 xERA), both players benefit from a significant 16% park boost and the high likelihood of successful swipes against Valdez\u2019s notoriously slow delivery to home plate.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today\u2019s lineup was omitting **Nolan Schanuel** (53.06) in favor of the current outfield and utility configuration. **Nolan Schanuel** was on the bubble, but his exposure to MacKenzie Gore (xERA 3.87) and the lack of a defined platoon advantage ultimately tipped the scale toward **Coby Mayo**, whose park-adjusted ceiling in this specific matchup is more conducive to our goals in HR and RBI. We are currently carrying significant risk regarding \"Lineup Pending\" statuses; specifically, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Gage Workman**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Sam Antonacci** are all projected based on assumed batting orders. Should **Sam Antonacci** slide down the lineup or **Gage Workman** fail to secure a start, we may need to pivot to the bench. Owners should keep a close watch on **Sam Antonacci** in particular; despite a lower base score, his elite 0.400 xwOBA and favorable wind conditions make him a high-leverage target if his leadoff position is confirmed.",
